                </table>
              </defaultValue>
            </field>
          </fields>
          <validators contentType="base64">HEseHQ==</validators>
        </format>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <int>1</int>
        <format maxRecords="2147483647">
          <fields>
            <field description="Channel Name" keyfield="true" name="name" nullable="true" type="S">
              <validators contentType="base64">HEweMSAyMTQ3NDgzNjQ3HRxSHlx3K15eTmFtZSBtYXkgY29udGFpbiBvbmx5IExhdGluIGxldHRlcnMsIGRpZ2l0cywgYW5kIHVuZGVyc2NvcmVzHQ==</validators>
              <help>This is a unique channel ID used to refer to channel data.</help>
              <defaultValue>
                <nullValue/>
              </defaultValue>
            </field>
            <field description="Variable" extendableSelectionValues="true" icon="fi_variable" name="variable" type="S">
              <help>Name of the variable whose value will be used in the statistical channel.</help>
              <defaultValue/>
            </field>
            <field description="Enabled" name="enabled" type="B">
              <help>Controls whether the channel is active and collects data. Default channels should be disabled instead of deleting them in order to prevent their recreation.</help>
              <defaultValue>1</defaultValue>
            </field>
            <field description="Parameters" icon="var_statistics" name="parameters" nullable="true" type="T">
              <help>These are parameters of statistical data collection, storage and processing.</help>
              <defaultValue>
                <table>
                  <format maxRecords="1" minRecords="1">
                    <fields>
                      <field description="Expression" editor="expression" name="expression" type="S">
                        <help>The &lt;b&gt;Expression&lt;/b&gt; property defines what data is the base of statistics. It is evaluated on every change of variable that the channel is built upon.The expression must evaluate to a number (integer of floating point). If the expression evaluates to any other data type, the system tries to convert it to a number and skips the value if conversion fails. If the expression evaluates to NULL, the system applies &lt;b&gt;NULL Value Handling&lt;/b&gt; method to it.</help>
                        <defaultValue/>
                      </field>
                      <field description="Average" name="average" type="B">
                        <help>This function calculates an average of Primary Data Points to form a Consolidated Data Point. This is an average of values themselves (for &lt;a href=&quot;doc://ls_internals_statistics_channel_types&quot;&gt;Gauge&lt;/a&gt; channel) or value change rates (for &lt;a href=&quot;doc://ls_internals_statistics_channel_types&quot;&gt;Counter&lt;/a&gt; and other channel types).</help>
                        <group>Aggregation</group>
                        <defaultValue>1</defaultValue>
                      </field>
                      <field description="Minimum" name="minimum" type="B">
                        <help>This function takes finds the minimal Primary Data Point to use as a Consolidated Data Point. This is minimal value itself (for &lt;a href=&quot;doc://ls_internals_statistics_channel_types&quot;&gt;Gauge&lt;/a&gt; channel) or minimal value change rate (for &lt;a href=&quot;doc://ls_internals_statistics_channel_types&quot;&gt;Counter&lt;/a&gt; and other channel types).</help>
                        <group>Aggregation</group>
                        <defaultValue>1</defaultValue>
                      </field>
                      <field description="Maximum" name="maximum" type="B">
                        <help>Similar to &lt;b&gt;Minimum&lt;/b&gt;.</help>
                        <group>Aggregation</group>
                        <defaultValue>1</defaultValue>
                      </field>
                      <field description="Total" name="total" type="B">
                        <help>This function sums all Primary Data Points to form a Consolidated Data Point. This is a sum of values themselves (for &lt;a href=&quot;doc://ls_internals_statistics_channel_types&quot;&gt;Gauge&lt;/a&gt; channel) or value change rates (for &lt;a href=&quot;doc://ls_internals_statistics_channel_types&quot;&gt;Counter&lt;/a&gt; and other channel types).</help>
                        <group>Aggregation</group>
                        <defaultValue>1</defaultValue>
                      </field>
                      <field description="First" name="first" type="B">
                        <help>This function takes first Primary Data Point as the value for a Consolidated Data Point.</help>
                        <group>Aggregation</group>
                        <defaultValue>0</defaultValue>
                      </field>
                      <field description="Last" name="last" type="B">
                        <help>This function takes last Primary Data Point as the value for a Consolidated Data Point.</help>
                        <group>Aggregation</group>
                        <defaultValue>0</defaultValue>
                      </field>
                      <field description="Minutely" editor="period" name="minutelyStats" nullable="true" type="L">
                        <editorOptions>2 3</editorOptions>
                        <validators contentType="base64">HEweMTIwMDAwIDkyMjMzNzIwMzY4NTQ3NzU4MDcd</validators>
                        <help>Storage period for minutely aggregates.</help>
                        <group>Storage Periods</group>
                        <defaultValue>3600000</defaultValue>
                      </field>
                      <field description="Hourly" editor="period" name="hourlyStats" nullable="true" type="L">
                        <editorOptions>3 4</editorOptions>
                        <validators contentType="base64">HEweNzIwMDAwMCA5MjIzMzcyMDM2ODU0Nzc1ODA3HQ==</validators>
                        <help>Storage period for hourly aggregates.</help>
                        <group>Storage Periods</group>
                        <defaultValue>86400000</defaultValue>
                      </field>
                      <field description="Daily" editor="period" name="dailyStats" nullable="true" type="L">
                        <editorOptions>4 6</editorOptions>
                        <validators contentType="base64">HEweMTcyODAwMDAwIDkyMjMzNzIwMzY4NTQ3NzU4MDcd</validators>
                        <help>Storage period for daily aggregates.</help>
                        <group>Storage Periods</group>
                        <defaultValue>2592000000</defaultValue>
                      </field>
                      <field description="Weekly" editor="period" name="weeklyStats" nullable="true" type="L">
                        <editorOptions>5 8</editorOptions>
                        <validators contentType="base64">HEweMTIwOTYwMDAwMCA5MjIzMzcyMDM2ODU0Nzc1ODA3HQ==</validators>
                        <help>Storage period for weekly aggregates.</help>
                        <group>Storage Periods</group>
                        <defaultValue>7776000000</defaultValue>
                      </field>
                      <field description="Monthly" editor="period" name="monthlyStats" nullable="true" type="L">
                        <editorOptions>6 8</editorOptions>
                        <validators contentType="base64">HEweNTE4NDAwMDAwMCA5MjIzMzcyMDM2ODU0Nzc1ODA3HQ==</validators>
                        <help>Storage period for monthly aggregates.</help>
                        <group>Storage Periods</group>
                        <defaultValue>31536000000</defaultValue>
                      </field>
                      <field description="Yearly" editor="period" name="yearlyStats" nullable="true" type="L">
                        <editorOptions>8 8</editorOptions>
                        <validators contentType="base64">HEweNjMwNzIwMDAwMDAgOTIyMzM3MjAzNjg1NDc3NTgwNx0=</validators>
                        <help>Storage period for yearly aggregates.</help>
                        <group>Storage Periods</group>
                        <defaultValue>315360000000</defaultValue>
                      </field>
                      <field description="Timestamp Expression" editor="expression" name="timestampExpression" nullable="true" type="S">
                        <help>Use this expression to override a default timestamp for each new variable value. The expression should evaluate to Date type.</help>
                        <group>Advanced Properties</group>
                        <defaultValue>{#timestamp}</defaultValue>
                      </field>
                      <field description="Use Key Field" name="useKeyField" type="B">
                        <help>If Use Key Field is disabled (the default setting), a single Dataset (i.e. set of statistical data) is created for this channel. If Use Key Field is enabled, one Dataset is created for every record in the source variable&apos;s value. Enabling this option has sense only for channels based on tabular variables. The name of dataset is defined by the unique record key constructed according to Key Field property.</help>
                        <defaultValue>0</defaultValue>
                      </field>
                      <field description="Key Field" name="keyField" nullable="true" type="S">
                        <help>Autodetect if value is NULL</help>
                        <defaultValue>
                          <nullValue/>
                        </defaultValue>
                      </field>
                      <field description="NULL Value Processing" name="nullValuesProcessing" type="I">
                        <selectionValues>
                          <option description="Discard">1</option>
                          <option description="Treat As Zero">2</option>
                        </selectionValues>
                        <help>&lt;p&gt;This setting defines that should the channel do when its &lt;b&gt;Expression&lt;/b&gt; was evaluated to NULL. There are two options:&lt;/p&gt; &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Discard&lt;/b&gt;. Value will be silently dropped. If no other values were received for a certain period, channel overall value becomes UNDEFINED for this period.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Treat As Zero&lt;/b&gt;. NULL values will be converted to zeros.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</help>
                        <defaultValue>1</defaultValue>
                      </field>
                      <field description="Out Of Range Value Processing" name="outOfRangeValuesHandling" type="I">
                        <selectionValues>
                          <option description="Do Nothing">0</option>
                          <option description="Discard">1</option>
                          <option description="Normalize">3</option>
                        </selectionValues>
                        <help>&lt;p&gt;Specifies how to process the values that are less than &lt;b&gt;Minimum Value&lt;/b&gt; or greater than &lt;b&gt;Maximum Value&lt;/b&gt;. The following choices are available:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Do Nothing&lt;/b&gt;. Simply disables minimum/maximum values for the channel.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Discard&lt;b&gt;. Drops values that are less than minimum or greater than maximum. If no other values were received for a certain period, channel overall value becomes UNDEFINED for this period.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Normalize&lt;b&gt;. Values less than minimum and greater than maximum are converted to the minimum and maximum values respectively.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</help>
                        <defaultValue>0</defaultValue>
                      </field>
                      <field description="Minimum Value" name="minValue" type="E">
                        <defaultValue>0</defaultValue>
                      </field>
                      <field description="Maximum Value" name="maxValue" type="E">
                        <defaultValue>1</defaultValue>
                      </field>
                      <field description="Storage" name="storage" type="I">
                        <selectionValues>
                          <option description="Standard file (Low memory usage, slow)">0</option>
                          <option description="Mapped file (High memory usage, fast)">1</option>
                          <option description="Memory (Non-persistent)">2</option>
                          <option description="NoSQL Storage">3</option>
                        </selectionValues>
                        <help>&lt;p&gt;Storage property defines statistics storage type. There are several options:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Mapped file (Higher memory usage, faster) - the default setting.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Standard file (Lower memory usage, slower).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Memory. Memory based storage guarantees maximum performance, but it doesn&apos;t preserve data between server restarts and, therefore, has very limited uses.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;NoSQL Storage. Leverages database-level failover, but is much slower compared to file storage.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</help>
                        <defaultValue>1</defaultValue>
                      </field>
                      <field description="Type" name="type" type="S">
                        <selectionValues>
                          <option description="Gauge">GAUGE</option>
                          <option description="Counter">COUNTER</option>
                          <option description="Derive">DERIVE</option>
                          <option description="Absolute">ABSOLUTE</option>
                        </selectionValues>
                        <help>The channel &lt;b&gt;Type&lt;/b&gt; setting defines how are subsequent source values processed to form &lt;a href=&quot;doc://ls_internals_statistics_rrd&quot;&gt;Primary Data&lt;/a&gt; Points for the channel.</help>
                        <defaultValue>GAUGE</defaultValue>
                      </field>
                      <field description="Protect Statistics" name="protectStatistics" type="B">
                        <help>Disable parameters that change resets statistics data</help>
                        <group>Advanced Properties</group>
                        <defaultValue>1</defaultValue>
                      </field>
                      <field description="Step" editor="period" name="step" type="L">
                        <editorOptions>1 1</editorOptions>
                        <validators contentType="base64">HEweMSA5MjIzMzcyMDM2ODU0Nzc1ODA3HQ==</validators>
                        <help>Changing this value resets statistics data</help>
                        <group>Advanced Properties</group>
                        <defaultValue>60000</defaultValue>
                      </field>
                      <field description="XFiles Factor" name="xff" type="F">
                        <validators contentType="base64">HEweMC4wIDAuOTk5HQ==</validators>
                        <help>Changing this value resets statistics data</help>
                        <group>Advanced Properties</group>
                        <defaultValue>0.9</defaultValue>
                      </field>
                      <field description="Heartbeat" editor="period" name="heartbeat" type="L">
                        <validators contentType="base64">HEweMCA5MjIzMzcyMDM2ODU0Nzc1ODA3HQ==</validators>
                        <help>The maximum time period that may pass between two updates of this data source before the value of the data source is assumed to be &apos;unknown&apos;. &apos;0&apos; means automatic heartbeat.</help>
                        <group>Advanced Properties</group>
                        <defaultValue>0</defaultValue>
                      </field>
                      <field description="Data Life Span for Missing Keys" editor="period" name="missedKeysLifespan" type="L">
                        <validators contentType="base64">HEweMCA5MjIzMzcyMDM2ODU0Nzc1ODA3HQ==</validators>
                        <help>Time period for that a data archive for a missing key will be stored. If the key is missing for a period shorter than that and then reappear, its associated data will survive. Zero value means removing data just once the the key is disappeared</help>
                        <group>Advanced Properties</group>
                        <defaultValue>1209600000</defaultValue>
                      </field>
                    </fields>
                    <bindings>
                      <binding>
                        <reference>keyField#hidden</reference>
                        <expression>!{useKeyField}</expression>
                      </binding>
                      <binding>
                        <reference>minValue#hidden</reference>
                        <expression>{outOfRangeValuesHandling} == 0</expression>
                      </binding>
                      <binding>
                        <reference>maxValue#hidden</reference>
                        <expression>{outOfRangeValuesHandling} == 0</expression>
                      </binding>
                      <binding>
                        <reference>step#enabled</reference>
                        <expression>!{protectStatistics}</expression>
                      </binding>
                      <binding>
                        <reference>xff#enabled</reference>
                        <expression>!{protectStatistics}</expression>
                      </binding>
                      <binding>
                        <reference>expression#options</reference>
                        <expression>hasResolver(&apos;parent&apos;) ? ({.:childInfo$type[0]} != 1 &amp;&amp; !variableAvailable({.:},{parent/variable}) ? cell(callFunction({.:}, &apos;expressionEditorOptions&apos;,{.:}, {parent/variable})):expressionEditorOptions({.:}, {parent/variable}, 1)): null</expression>
                      </binding>
                    </bindings>
                    <validators contentType="base64">HEUeZTIxcGJsWmhiSFZsZlNBOElIdHRZWGhXWVd4MVpYMGdQeUJ1ZFd4c0lEb2dKMDFwYm1sdGRXMGdWbUZzZFdVZ2MyaHZkV3hrSUdKbElHeGxjM05sY2lCMGFHRnVJRTFoZUdsdGRXMGdWbUZzZFdVbh0=</validators>
                  </format>
                  <records>
                    <record>
                      <value name="timestampExpression">
                        <nullValue/>
                      </value>
                    </record>
                  </records>
                </table>
              </defaultValue>
            </field>
            <field description="Inherited Property" name="inheritedMark" type="B">
              <help>Marked properties will be changed accordingly with their parents</help>
              <defaultValue>0</defaultValue>
            </field>
            <field description="Parent Model" hidden="true" name="parent" nullable="true" type="S">
              <defaultValue>
                <nullValue/>
              </defaultValue>
            </field>
          </fields>
          <bindings>
            <binding>
              <reference>variable#choices</reference>
              <expression>callFunction({.:}, &apos;variablesByMask&apos;,{.:})</expression>
            </binding>
          </bindings>
          <validators contentType="base64">HEseHQ==</validators>
        </format>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <int>2</int>
        <format maxRecords="1" minRecords="1">
          <fields>
            <field description="Name" name="name" notReplicated="true" type="S">
              <validators contentType="base64">HEkeHRxMHjEgNTAdHFIeXHcrXl5OYW1lIG1heSBjb250YWluIG9ubHkgTGF0aW4gbGV0dGVycywgZGlnaXRzLCBhbmQgdW5kZXJzY29yZXMd</validators>
              <help>Name of the resource and corresponding system context, required to refer to this resource from other parts of the system. It should satisfy the context naming conventions. WARNING: changing name will corrupt all references to the resource.</help>
              <defaultValue/>
            </field>
            <field description="Description" name="description" notReplicated="true" type="S">
              <validators contentType="base64">HEweMCAxMDAdHFIeW15ccHtDbnRybH1dKl5eRGVzY3JpcHRpb24gbWF5IGNvbnRhaW4gb25seSBwcmludGFibGUgY2hhcmFjdGVycx0=</validators>
              <help>The model context description (the text is displayed in the context tree).</help>
              <defaultValue/>
            </field>
            <field description="Type" name="type" type="I">
              <selectionValues>
                <option description="Relative">0</option>
                <option description="Absolute">1</option>
                <option description="Instantiable">2</option>
              </selectionValues>
              <help>This option specifies the model type: Relative, Absolute or Instantiable.</help>
              <defaultValue>1</defaultValue>
            </field>
            <field description="Validity Expression" editor="expression" name="validityExpression" type="S">
              <editorOptions contentType="base64"></editorOptions>
              <help>Acts differently for relative and instantiable model types. For a relative model, determines which context(s) should the model attach to. For an instantiable model, determines which context(s) should model instance containers be attached to.</help>
              <group>Validity</group>
              <defaultValue/>
            </field>
            <field description="Validity Update Rules" name="validityListeners" type="T">
              <help>A list of context masks and event names. If event specified by Event field of this table occurs in any of context matching to the mask specified by Mask field in the same record, Validity Expression will be recalculated for this context. This allows to make model valid or invalid for a certain context if some changes occur in it.</help>
              <group>Validity</group>
              <defaultValue>
                <table>
                  <format maxRecords="2147483647">
                    <fields>
                      <field description="Context Mask" editor="contextmask" icon="fi_context" keyfield="true" name="mask" type="S">
                        <help>Mask of contexts to monitor events in</help>
                        <defaultValue/>
                      </field>
                      <field description="Event" extendableSelectionValues="true" icon="fi_event" keyfield="true" name="event" type="S">
                        <help>Name of Event to listen for</help>
                        <defaultValue/>
                      </field>
                      <field description="Target Expression" editor="expression" icon="fi_expression" name="expression" nullable="true" type="S">
                        <editorOptions contentType="base64"></editorOptions>
                        <help>If specified, points to a context those validity should be checked. If Target Expression is not specified (what is suitable in most cases), the system checks validity of context in that Event has occurred.</help>
                        <defaultValue>
                          <nullValue/>
                        </defaultValue>
                      </field>
                    </fields>
                    <bindings>
                      <binding>
                        <reference>event#choices</reference>
                        <expression>{utilities:eventsByMask(&apos;{mask}&apos;)}</expression>
                      </binding>
                    </bindings>
                    <validators contentType="base64">HEseHQ==</validators>
                  </format>
                </table>
              </defaultValue>
            </field>
            <field description="Container Type" name="containerType" type="S">
              <validators contentType="base64">HEweMSA1MB0cUh5cdyteXlR5cGUgbWF5IGNvbnRhaW4gb25seSBsZXR0ZXJzLCBkaWdpdHMsIGFuZCB1bmRlcnNjb3Jlcx0=</validators>
              <help>This option defines the context type of the model containers. The Type string can include only English letters, numbers and underscores.</help>
              <group>Instantiable Model Settings</group>
              <defaultValue>objects</defaultValue>
            </field>
            <field description="Container Type Description" name="containerTypeDescription" type="S">
              <validators contentType="base64">HEweMCAxMDAdHFIeW15ccHtDbnRybH1dKl5eRGVzY3JpcHRpb24gbWF5IGNvbnRhaW4gb25seSBwcmludGFibGUgY2hhcmFjdGVycx0=</validators>
              <help>This option defines a human-readable description of the model container context type.</help>
              <group>Instantiable Model Settings</group>
              <defaultValue>Objects</defaultValue>
            </field>
            <field description="Container Name" name="containerName" type="S">
              <validators contentType="base64">HEweMSA1MB0cUh5cdyteXk5hbWUgbWF5IGNvbnRhaW4gb25seSBMYXRpbiBsZXR0ZXJzLCBkaWdpdHMsIGFuZCB1bmRlcnNjb3Jlcx0=</validators>
              <help>This option defines the context name of the model containers. It should satisfy the context naming conventions.</help>
              <group>Instantiable Model Settings</group>
              <defaultValue>objects</defaultValue>
            </field>
            <field description="Default Context" editor="context" name="defaultContext" nullable="true" type="S">
              <help>Default context which is used in all internal expressions.</help>
              <group>Validity</group>
              <defaultValue>
                <nullValue/>
              </defaultValue>
            </field>
            <field description="Object Type" name="objectType" type="S">
              <validators contentType="base64">HEweMSA1MB0cUh5cdyteXlR5cGUgbWF5IGNvbnRhaW4gb25seSBsZXR0ZXJzLCBkaWdpdHMsIGFuZCB1bmRlcnNjb3Jlcx0=</validators>
              <help>This option is applicable to instantiable models only. It defines the context type of the model instances. The Type string can include only English letters, numbers and underscores.</help>
              <group>Instantiable Model Settings</group>
              <defaultValue>object</defaultValue>
            </field>
            <field description="Object Type Description" name="objectTypeDescription" type="S">
              <help>This option is applicable to instantiable models only. It defines a human-readable description of the model instance context type.</help>
              <group>Instantiable Model Settings</group>
              <defaultValue>Object</defaultValue>
            </field>
            <field description="Object Naming Expression" editor="expression" name="objectNamingExpression" type="S">
              <editorOptions contentType="base64"></editorOptions>
              <help>This option is applicable to instantiable models only. It defines description of the instantiable model&apos;s context.</help>
              <group>Instantiable Model Settings</group>
              <defaultValue/>
            </field>
            <field advanced="true" description="Enabled" name="enabled" type="B">
              <help>If this flag is unchecked, the model is deactivated and doesn&apos;t perform any active binding processing. However, all variables, function and event definitions added by this model remain available if the model is disabled. Instances of a disabled instantiable model are also not hidden or removed from server context tree.</help>
              <defaultValue>1</defaultValue>
            </field>
            <field advanced="true" description="Parent Models" name="parentModels" type="T">
              <help>Parent Models that entities (variables, functions, events, bindings, rule sets) will be inherited by the model.</help>
              <defaultValue>
                <table>
                  <format maxRecords="2147483647">
                    <fields>
                      <field description="Context" editor="context" name="parent" type="S">
                        <editorOptions contentType="base64"></editorOptions>
                        <defaultValue/>
                      </field>
                    </fields>
                  </format>
                </table>
              </defaultValue>
            </field>
            <field advanced="true" description="Generate Attached and Detached Events" name="generateAttachedEvents" type="B">
              <help>Attached and Detached events to be generated after attaching to a context</help>
              <defaultValue>0</defaultValue>
            </field>
            <field advanced="true" description="Rule Set Call Stack Depth Threshold" name="ruleSetCallStackDepthThreshold" type="I">
              <validators contentType="base64">HEweMSAyMTQ3NDgzNjQ3HQ==</validators>
              <help>An Information event is generated in this model (and a record is made in the Server log) if the rule set call stack depth exceeds the value defined by this option. This can happen when a rule set is called recursively.</help>
              <defaultValue>100</defaultValue>
            </field>
            <field advanced="true" description="Allow Spreadsheets In Instances" name="allowSpreadsheetsInInstances" type="B">
              <help>This option is applicable to relative and instantiable models only. It indicates whether to copy or not spreadsheet(s) to model instance.</help>
              <defaultValue>0</defaultValue>
            </field>
            <field advanced="true" description="Normal Concurrent Bindings" name="normalConcurrentBindings" type="I">
              <help>This option defines the core size of the model thread pool, i.e. the standard bindings count processed simultaneously.</help>
              <group>Advanced Binding Settings</group>
              <defaultValue>3</defaultValue>
            </field>
            <field advanced="true" description="Maximum Concurrent Bindings" name="maximumConcurrentBindings" type="I">
              <validators contentType="base64">HEweMSAyMTQ3NDgzNjQ3HQ==</validators>
              <help>This option defines the maximum size of the model thread pool, i.e. the number of concurrently processed bindings allowed in case the binding queue overflows.</help>
              <group>Advanced Binding Settings</group>
              <defaultValue>30</defaultValue>
            </field>
            <field advanced="true" description="Maximum Unprocessed Binding Queue Length" name="maximumBindingQueueLength" type="I">
              <help>This option defines how many unprocessed binding operations can be queued before the model&apos;s thread pool size exceeds its core size in relation to the maximum size.</help>
              <group>Advanced Binding Settings</group>
              <defaultValue>100</defaultValue>
            </field>
            <field advanced="true" description="Log Bindings Execution" name="logBindingsExecution" type="B">
              <help>This option enables and disables the logging of all executed bindings.</help>
              <group>Advanced Binding Settings</group>
              <defaultValue>0</defaultValue>
            </field>
            <field hidden="true" name="protected" type="B">
              <defaultValue>0</defaultValue>
            </field>
          </fields>
          <bindings>
            <binding>
              <reference>validityExpression#hidden</reference>
              <expression>{type} == 1</expression>
            </binding>
            <binding>
              <reference>validityListeners#hidden</reference>
              <expression>{type} == 1</expression>
            </binding>
            <binding>
              <reference>generateAttachedEvents#hidden</reference>
              <expression>{type} == 1</expression>
            </binding>
            <binding>
              <reference>containerType#hidden</reference>
              <expression>{type} != 2</expression>
            </binding>
            <binding>
              <reference>containerTypeDescription#hidden</reference>
              <expression>{type} != 2</expression>
            </binding>
            <binding>
              <reference>containerName#hidden</reference>
              <expression>{type} != 2</expression>
            </binding>
            <binding>
              <reference>objectType#hidden</reference>
              <expression>{type} != 2</expression>
            </binding>
            <binding>
              <reference>objectTypeDescription#hidden</reference>
              <expression>{type} != 2</expression>
            </binding>
            <binding>
              <reference>objectNamingExpression#hidden</reference>
              <expression>{type} != 2</expression>
            </binding>
            <binding>
              <reference>defaultContext#hidden</reference>
              <expression>{type} != 0</expression>
            </binding>
            <binding>
              <reference>validityExpression#options</reference>
              <expression>expressionEditorOptions({type} == 0 ? {defaultContext} : {.:})</expression>
            </binding>
            <binding>
              <reference>allowSpreadsheetsInInstances#hidden</reference>
              <expression>{type} == 1</expression>
            </binding>
          </bindings>
          <validators contentType="base64">HEUeZTIxaGVHbHRkVzFEYjI1amRYSnlaVzUwUW1sdVpHbHVaM045SUQ0OUlIdHViM0p0WVd4RGIyNWpkWEp5Wlc1MFFtbHVaR2x1WjNOOUlEOGdiblZzYkNBNklDZE5ZWGhwYlhWdElHTnZibU4xY25KbGJuUWdZbWx1WkdsdVp5QmpiM1Z1ZENCdGRYTjBJR0psSUdkeVpXRjBaWElnYjNJZ1pYRjFZV3dnZEc4Z2JtOXliV0ZzSUdOdmJtTjFjbkpsYm5RZ1ltbHVaR2x1WnlCamIzVnVkQ2M9HQ==</validators>
        </format>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <int>3</int>
        <format maxRecords="2147483647" reorderable="true">
          <fields>
            <field hidden="true" name="bindingId" notReplicated="true" nullable="true" type="L">
              <validators contentType="base64">HEweMCA5MjIzMzcyMDM2ODU0Nzc1ODA3HQ==</validators>
              <defaultValue>
                <nullValue/>
              </defaultValue>
            </field>
            <field description="Target" editor="target" name="target" type="S">
              <editorOptions>models</editorOptions>
              <help>A reference that points to where the evaluation result of a binding Expression will be applied/stored.</help>
              <defaultValue/>
            </field>
            <field description="Expression" editor="expression" name="expression" type="S">
              <editorOptions contentType="base64"></editorOptions>
              <help>An expression that is evaluated every time the binding is processed. Its evaluation result is stored in binding Target.</help>
              <defaultValue/>
            </field>
            <field description="Activator" editor="activator" name="activator" type="S">
              <help>A reference that points to some event or variable (property). Occurrence of this event or change of this variable (property) triggers processing of the binding. If activator is not specified and On Event flag is set, the binding will be processed when any component of its Expression changes.</help>
              <defaultValue/>
            </field>
            <field description="Condition" editor="expression" name="condition" type="S">
              <editorOptions contentType="base64"></editorOptions>
              <help>An expression that is evaluated upon binding activation. The evaluation result should be a boolean that indicates whether the binding should be processed or not.</help>
              <defaultValue/>
            </field>
            <field description="On Startup" name="onstartup" type="B">
              <help>When enabled, the binding is processed once the widget is launched.</help>
              <defaultValue>0</defaultValue>
            </field>
            <field description="On Event" name="onevent" type="B">
              <help>When enabled, the binding is processed upon Activator event (or Activator state change, if activator is a property). If Activator is not specified, the binding is processed when any component of the Expression changes.</help>
              <defaultValue>0</defaultValue>
            </field>
            <field description="Periodically" name="periodically" type="B">
              <help>When enabled, the binding will be processed periodically.</help>
              <defaultValue>0</defaultValue>
            </field>
            <field description="Period" editor="period" name="period" type="L">
              <validators contentType="base64">HEweMSA5MjIzMzcyMDM2ODU0Nzc1ODA3HQ==</validators>
              <help>Interval between periodical binding executions.</help>
              <defaultValue>60000</defaultValue>
            </field>
            <field advanced="true" description="Queue" hidden="true" name="queue" type="S">
              <validators contentType="base64">HFIeXHcqXl5OYW1lIG1heSBjb250YWluIG9ubHkgTGF0aW4gbGV0dGVycywgZGlnaXRzLCBhbmQgdW5kZXJzY29yZXMd</validators>
              <help>Target operations of bindings in the same queue are guaranteed to be performed sequentially.</help>
              <defaultValue/>
            </field>
            <field description="Inherited Property" name="inheritedMark" type="B">
              <help>Marked properties will be changed accordingly with their parents</help>
              <defaultValue>0</defaultValue>
            </field>
            <field description="Parent Model" hidden="true" name="parent" type="S">
              <defaultValue>false</defaultValue>
            </field>
          </fields>
          <bindings>
            <binding>
              <reference>activator#enabled</reference>
              <expression>{onevent}</expression>
            </binding>
            <binding>
              <reference>period#enabled</reference>
              <expression>{periodically}</expression>
            </binding>
            <binding>
              <reference>bindingId</reference>
              <expression>{bindingId}==null ? long(random()*9223372036854775807) : {bindingId}</expression>
            </binding>
            <binding>
              <reference>target#options</reference>
              <expression>expressionEditorOptions({childInfo$type[0]} == 0 ? {childInfo$defaultContext[0]} : {.:})</expression>
            </binding>
            <binding>
              <reference>expression#options</reference>
              <expression>expressionEditorOptions({childInfo$type[0]} == 0 ? {childInfo$defaultContext[0]} : {.:})</expression>
            </binding>
            <binding>
              <reference>activator#options</reference>
              <expression>expressionEditorOptions({childInfo$type[0]} == 0 ? {childInfo$defaultContext[0]} : {.:})</expression>
            </binding>
            <binding>
              <reference>condition#options</reference>
              <expression>expressionEditorOptions({childInfo$type[0]} == 0 ? {childInfo$defaultContext[0]} : {.:})</expression>
            </binding>
          </bindings>
        </format>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <int>4</int>
        <format maxRecords="2147483647" reorderable="true">
          <fields>
            <field description="Name" keyfield="true" name="name" type="S">
              <validators contentType="base64">HEweMSA1MB0cUh5cdyteXk5hbWUgbWF5IGNvbnRhaW4gb25seSBMYXRpbiBsZXR0ZXJzLCBkaWdpdHMsIGFuZCB1bmRlcnNjb3Jlcx0=</validators>
              <help>This field defines the function name.</help>
              <defaultValue/>
            </field>
            <field description="Description" name="description" nullable="true" type="S">
              <validators contentType="base64">HEweMSAxMDAdHFIeW15ccHtDbnRybH1dKl5eRGVzY3JpcHRpb24gbWF5IGNvbnRhaW4gb25seSBwcmludGFibGUgY2hhcmFjdGVycx0=</validators>
              <help>This field is used to set a human-readable function description.</help>
              <defaultValue>
                <nullValue/>
              </defaultValue>
            </field>
            <field description="Input Format" name="inputformat" type="T">
              <help>This field is used to define the function input format.</help>
              <defaultValue>
                <table>
                  <format maxRecords="1" minRecords="1" namingExpression="print({fields}, &apos;{name}&apos;, &apos;, &apos;)">
                    <fields>
                      <field description="Minimal Record Count" name="minRecords" type="I">
                        <validators contentType="base64">HEweMCAyMTQ3NDgzNjQ3HQ==</validators>
                        <help>The number of records should be within this range, otherwise the table will be treated as &lt;i&gt;invalid&lt;/i&gt;.</help>
                        <defaultValue>0</defaultValue>
                      </field>
                      <field description="Maximal Record Count" extendableSelectionValues="true" name="maxRecords" type="I">
                        <validators contentType="base64">HEweMCAyMTQ3NDgzNjQ3HQ==</validators>
                        <selectionValues>
                          <option description="Not limited">2147483647</option>
                        </selectionValues>
                        <help>The number of records should be within this range, otherwise the table will be treated as &lt;i&gt;invalid&lt;/i&gt;.</help>
                        <defaultValue>2147483647</defaultValue>
                      </field>
                      <field description="Fields" name="fields" type="T">
                        <help>Each row in this property defines a field of the data table.</help>
                        <defaultValue>
                          <table>
                            <format maxRecords="2147483647" reorderable="true">
                              <fields>
                                <field hidden="true" name="oldname" type="S">
                                  <defaultValue/>
                                </field>
                                <field description="Name" keyfield="true" name="name" type="S">
                                  <validators contentType="base64">HFIeXHcrXl5OYW1lIG1heSBjb250YWluIG9ubHkgTGF0aW4gbGV0dGVycywgZGlnaXRzLCBhbmQgdW5kZXJzY29yZXMd</validators>
                                  <help>Name of the field. The name is used to refer the field.</help>
                                  <defaultValue/>
                                </field>
                                <field description="Type" name="type" type="S">
                                  <selectionValues>
                                    <option description="Integer">I</option>
                                    <option description="String">S</option>
                                    <option description="Boolean">B</option>
                                    <option description="Long">L</option>
                                    <option description="Float">F</option>
                                    <option description="Double">E</option>
                                    <option description="Date">D</option>
                                    <option description="Data Table">T</option>
                                    <option description="Color">C</option>
                                    <option description="Data Block">A</option>
                                  </selectionValues>
                                  <help>Type of the field.</help>
                                  <defaultValue>I</defaultValue>
                                </field>
                                <field description="Description" name="description" nullable="true" type="S">
                                  <validators contentType="base64">HFIeW15ccHtDbnRybH1dKl5eRGVzY3JpcHRpb24gbWF5IGNvbnRhaW4gb25seSBwcmludGFibGUgY2hhcmFjdGVycx0=</validators>
                                  <help>Textual field description.</help>
                                  <defaultValue>
                                    <nullValue/>
                                  </defaultValue>
                                </field>
                                <field description="Default" name="defaultValue" nullable="true" type="S">
                                  <help>Default value of the field. You can omit this only if the field is nullable.</help>
                                  <defaultValue>
                                    <nullValue/>
                                  </defaultValue>
                                </field>
                                <field description="Read-only" name="readonly" type="B">
                                  <help>Flag indicating that the values in this field are read-only. This applied to the UI-level editing and some data model level operations as well.</help>
                                  <defaultValue>0</defaultValue>
                                </field>
                                <field description="Nullable" name="nullable" type="B">
                                  <help>Flag indicating that field can contain NULL values.</help>
                                  <defaultValue>0</defaultValue>
                                </field>
                                <field description="Key" name="key" type="B">
                                  <help>Flag indicating that the field is a part of record’s unique ID, which is a unique combination of all key fields defined in the table format. Any declared key fields usually force the Data Table Smart Copy operation to employ a special copy algorithm that match records by their unique key field combinations rather than record numbers.</help>
                                  <defaultValue>0</defaultValue>
                                </field>
                                <field description="Selection Values" name="selvals" type="T">
                                  <help>List of values that can be selected for the field via a drop-down menu. A description must be defined for each value. Descriptions are shown when displaying the table to a user, and the values are available when the cell is referenced inside the platform.</help>
                                  <defaultValue>
                                    <table>
                                      <format maxRecords="2147483647" reorderable="true">
                                        <fields>
                                          <field description="Value" keyfield="true" name="value" nullable="true" type="S">
                                            <defaultValue>
                                              <nullValue/>
                                            </defaultValue>
                                          </field>
                                          <field description="Description" name="description" type="S">
                                            <defaultValue/>
                                          </field>
                                        </fields>
                                        <validators contentType="base64">HEseHQ==</validators>
                                      </format>
                                    </table>
                                  </defaultValue>
                                </field>
                                <field description="Extendable Selection Values" name="extselvals" type="B">
                                  <help>Flag indicating the field may be set to any value, including ones not listed in Selection Values.</help>
                                  <defaultValue>0</defaultValue>
                                </field>
                                <field advanced="true" description="Hidden" name="hidden" type="B">
                                  <help>The setting hides the field in the UI, but it remains accessible at the data model level.</help>
                                  <defaultValue>0</defaultValue>
                                </field>
                                <field advanced="true" description="Inline" name="inline" type="B">
                                  <help>&lt;p&gt;This flag has special meaning for different fields:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;If the Inline flag is set for a Data Block field, the field value will be stored in a dedicated database table. The value will not be initially loaded if the table itself is loaded from the database and sent to a AggreGate Client or external application. The Data Block value will, however, contain a data block ID that can be used to force loading the Data Block data from the server database. This is suitable for large binary values, such as image, sound, and video files.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;If Inline flag is set for a Color field, field value will be used to highlight records of the table when its being viewed/edited in a Data Table Editor. Its often feasible to combine Inline flag with a Hidden flag to hide the Color field itself from the table. See the Row Coloring section below for more information.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;If Inline flag is set for a Data Table field, default value of the field will have same format as format of the table to which the field belongs. This effectively enables creation of tables with unlimited nesting using Data Table Editor.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</help>
                                  <defaultValue>0</defaultValue>
                                </field>
                                <field advanced="true" description="Encrypted" name="encrypted" type="B">
                                  <help>Enables database-level field value encryption.</help>
                                  <defaultValue>0</defaultValue>
                                </field>
                                <field description="Help" editor="textarea" name="help" nullable="true" type="S">
                                  <validators contentType="base64">HFIeW15ccHtDbnRybH1dKl5eRGVzY3JpcHRpb24gbWF5IGNvbnRhaW4gb25seSBwcmludGFibGUgY2hhcmFjdGVycx0=</validators>
                                  <help>Contents of the pop-up which is displayed to the user when hovering over a field.</help>
                                  <defaultValue>
                                    <nullValue/>
                                  </defaultValue>
                                </field>
                                <field description="Editor/Viewer" extendableSelectionValues="true" name="editor" nullable="true" type="S">
